# A slow tool call, then a second message sent while Claude is still working (steering), then a
# two-line message typed with a lone newline write between the lines (Ctrl+J), never bracketed paste.
mark
wait 8000 Yes, I trust this folder
iffound send y
iffound sleep 150
iffound send \r
wait 6000 Keep xhigh
iffound send n
iffound sleep 150
iffound send \r
quiet 2500 30000
send Use the Bash tool to run the command: sleep 20. After it finishes reply with exactly OK DONE.
sleep 150
send \r
sleep 7000
send Second message sent while you were busy: after OK DONE also write the word HELLO on its own line.
sleep 150
send \r
mark
wait 120000 \x07
quiet 4000 60000
send Reply with the number of lines in this message and the text of its last line.
sleep 100
send \n
sleep 100
send This is the second line.
sleep 150
send \r
mark
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 3000 30000
send /exit
sleep 150
send \r
exit 15000
